.IX Title "AMSHELLO 1"
.TH AMSHELLO 1 2025-11-26 "perl v5.38.2" "AMS executables"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
amshello \- Asynchronous Message Service (AMS) demo program for UNIX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBamshello\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBamshello\fR is a sample program designed to demonstrate that an entire
(very simple) distributed AMS application can be written in just a few
lines of C code.  When started, \fBamshello\fR forks a second process and
initiates transmission of a "Hello" text message from one process to the
other, after which both processes unregister and terminate.
.PP
The \fBamshello\fR processes will register as application modules in the
root unit of the venture identified by application name "amsdemo" and
authority name "test".  A configuration server for the local continuum
and a registrar for the root unit of that venture (which may both be
instantiated in a single \fBamsd\fR daemon task) must be running in order
for the \fBamshello\fR processes to run.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBamshello\fR terminated normally.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
A MIB initialization file with the applicable default name (see \fBamsrc\fR\|(5))
must be present.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
